# Application Architecture

## Package Responsibilities

| Package | Responsibility |
|---------|---------------|
| `domain/` | Freezed models, repository interfaces — no Flutter deps |
| `data/` | DTOs, API providers (retrofit/dio), repository implementations, mappers |
| `core/` | DI setup, BLoC base classes, utilities, shared services |
| `core_ui/` | Design system widgets, theme, reusable UI components |
| `navigation/` | auto_route router, route guards, route definitions |
| `features/*/` | Feature-specific screens, BLoC, and widgets |

## Layer Rules

- `domain` must not depend on `data`, `core`, or any Flutter packages.
- `data` implements interfaces from `domain`; maps DTOs → domain models.
- `features` depend on `domain` and `core`; never import `data` directly.
- `core_ui` has no business logic; only UI and theme.

## Dependency Injection (injectable + get_it)

- Register all services and repositories with `@injectable`, `@singleton`, or `@lazySingleton`.
- Use `@module` for third-party registrations (Dio, SharedPreferences, etc.).
- Configure the DI container in `core/` using generated `injectable.config.dart`.
- Inject dependencies through constructors — never access `GetIt` directly inside widgets or BLoCs.

```dart
// ✅ Constructor injection via injectable
@injectable
class AuthRepository implements IAuthRepository {
  AuthRepository(this._apiProvider);
  final AuthApiProvider _apiProvider;
}
```

## Repository Pattern

- `domain/` defines abstract repository interfaces (`IAuthRepository`).
- `data/` provides concrete implementations (`AuthRepository`).
- BLoCs depend on domain interfaces, not data implementations.
- Map DTOs to domain models in repositories — BLoCs never see DTOs.

## Feature Module Structure

Each feature follows:

```
features/my_feature/
  lib/src/
    presentation/
      screens/       # Screens (one BLoC per screen)
      widgets/       # Private/reusable widgets for this feature
      bloc/          # BLoC + events + states
```
